# BUGS

A record devmgr cannot use is ignored: one with no program, with a PCI match that has neither `vendor` and `device` nor `class`, or with a value too long.
Nothing is said of any of them.

Any `match=` but `acpi` is taken as PCI, so `match=usb vendor=... device=...` matches PCI functions.

devmgr reads every file in `/boot/drv`, not only `.ndb` files, and at most 8 KiB of each.

`msi=` above 8 gives 8, `clock` on a PCI match does nothing, and a numbered post on an ACPI match is not numbered.
devmgr keeps 16 drivers, 8 ACPI matches and 64 PCI functions.

Every driver is restarted when it exits, up to five starts in all; a manifest cannot say otherwise.
The match manifest `docs/01-kernel-ipc.md` sketches, with `bus=dt`, `compatible=`, `intent=`, `trusted` and `switched=`, is not read: there is no device-tree bus, and no key for a driver's intent or trust.
